# L §5.9 One row replaced: "A later version may replace one row of a table ... from its governs; the table it
# gives is the earlier table with that row's value replaced, and its interval must be one of the earlier
# table's".  Written in the grammar's form (L §2.3 vitem: "replace" bandrow).  From 2027 the row (10, inf)
# gives 3; the row [0, 10] still gives 1; in 2026 the earlier table's row gives 2.
# held: (L §8.2) "a row whose span has a start and no end ..., band rows included, read at a law date after the
# cut K": the law date is after the model's on, so every open-ended row read is listed.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

source s "s"
band b(n: int): int
input lo: int
input hi: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  b: [0, 10] = 1
  b: (10, inf) = 2
  lo = 5
  hi = 50

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2027..
  known 2026-12-01
  replace b: (10, inf) = 3

ask q1: b(lo), b(hi) law 2027-06-30
ask q2: b(hi) law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: (1, 3)
  held: b row (10, inf) (v2), read for 2027-06-30
  held: b row [0, 10] (v1), read for 2027-06-30
  held: hi = 50 (v1), read for 2027-06-30
  held: lo = 5 (v1), read for 2027-06-30
  law date 2027-06-30, cut 2027-01-01
q2: 2
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2027-01-01
